  "estimatedLength": "60 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify and label the four chambers of the heart (right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium, left ventricle) and the major vessels entering and leaving the heart.",
    "Explain the sequence of blood flow through the heart and the role of the four valves in ensuring unidirectional flow.",
    "Describe the dual-loop circulation and the distinct roles of the right and left sides in pulmonary and systemic circuits.",
    "Compare the wall thickness of the left ventricle to the right ventricle and explain the functional implications for pumping to the systemic circulation.",
    "Demonstrate how heart valves prevent backflow during the cardiac cycle using visual cues."
  ],
